{"term":"brute","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cabe89b44ae904c00a","definition":"Without reason or intelligence (of animals).","example":"a brute beast","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["brute fact","brute strength"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:53b71d22651cfbf78f","definition":"Characteristic of unthinking animals; senseless, unreasoning (of humans).","example":"A creature […] not prone / And brute as other creatures, but endued / With sanctity of reason.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["brute fact","brute strength"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:45474cbac174274bd9","definition":"Unconnected with intelligence or thought; purely material, senseless.","example":"the brute earth; the brute powers of nature","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["brute fact","brute strength"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7b9f87d61a0e4748f1","definition":"Crude, unpolished.","example":"a great brute farmer from Liddesdale","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["brute fact","brute strength"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:da21badc38fcc57ebd","definition":"Strong, blunt, and spontaneous; being purely physical in nature.","example":"I got the door open through brute force.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["brute fact","brute strength"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7c28db80ea3f1c62c7","definition":"Brutal; cruel; fierce; ferocious; savage; pitiless, without intelligence or reason.","example":"brute violence","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["brute fact","brute strength"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:698d6753fb1a531f5c","definition":"An animal seen as being without human reason; a senseless beast.","example":"they laid before them how unbecoming it was the Dignity of such sublime Creatures to be sollicitous about gratifying those Appetites, which they had in common with Brutes, and at the same time unmindful of those higher qualities that gave them the preeminence over all visible Beings.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["brute fact","brute strength","brutal","brutality","brutedom","brute force","brute for punishment","brutelike","brutely","bruteness","bruter","brutesome","brutify","brutish","brutism","brutist","imbrute","unbrute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2c64f83fa6a3ab726c","definition":"A person with the characteristics of an unthinking animal; a coarse or brutal person, particularly one who is dim-witted.","example":"One of them was a hulking brute of a man, heavily tattooed and with a h